<%#
  LEGACY FIELD PARTIAL: metadata_field_component_sf
  STATUS: FULLY DEPRECATED - NO LONGER USED

  HISTORICAL CONTEXT:
  This partial was the original implementation for rendering subject_fast fields
  within the Blacklight::MetadataFieldComponent view structure (used for index/search results).

  ORIGINAL APPROACH:
  - Used render_async gem to asynchronously load subject term definitions
  - Configured with RenderAsync.configure do |config| config.jquery = true end
  - Relied on jQuery (window.jQuery) being available for AJAX requests
  - Called subject_path helper with URL parameter for async endpoint

  WHY NO LONGER USED:
  - jQuery was not properly exposed on window object
  - render_async JavaScript failed silently when jQuery unavailable
  - Result: Empty async placeholder divs in rendered HTML (no content loaded)
  - Deprecated in favor of direct rendering

  REPLACEMENT APPROACHES:
  1. Index/Search Results: Direct rendering in Blacklight::MetadataFieldComponent
     File: app/components/blacklight/metadata_field_component.html.erb
     Uses: OclcSubjectFastService for direct term fetching
     
  2. Show Page: Direct rendering in ERB partial
     File: app/views/catalog/_field_subject_fast.erb
     Uses: OclcSubjectFastService for direct term fetching

  CURRENT STATUS:
  - Both show page (_field_subject_fast.erb) and index context (metadata_field_component.html.erb)
    now use direct rendering with OclcSubjectFastService
  - No async rendering needed anymore
  - This file kept for historical reference only

  TO DELETE:
  This file can be safely deleted once the migration to direct rendering is confirmed stable.
%>
<% field.document[:subject_fast].each do |url| %>
  <%= render_async subject_path url:url %>
<% end %>